# Flow: Feature

Purpose:
  Feature implementation flow following SDDRA standard.
  Enforces BE->BE_TS->CR->FE->FE_TS->CR->MD->MD_TS->CR->BRU/CRU->MANUAL.

Flow:
  AN -> AR -> DB -> BE -> BE_TS -> CR -> FE -> FE_TS -> CR -> MD -> MD_TS -> CR -> BRU -> CRU -> MANUAL -> VR

  This is the mandatory flow for all feature work.
  Branches and merges follow branch hierarchy rules.

BranchMapping:
  BE:  MODUL/<backend_module> -> DEC/<id> -> TASK/<id>
  FE:  MODUL/<frontend_module> -> DEC/<id> -> TASK/<id>
  MD:  MODUL/<mobile_module> -> DEC/<id> -> TASK/<id>

TestStrategy:
  BE_TS: unit, integration, contract — only changed files
  FE_TS: component, integration, e2e — only changed files
  MD_TS: platform, integration, offline — only changed files

GateSequence:
  1. AN gate: scope documented
  2. AR gate: architecture decided
  3. DB gate: schema validated
  4. BE gate: code compiles, tests pass
  5. BE_TS gate: backend tests pass
  6. CR gate: code review passed
  7. FE gate: UI builds, tests pass
  8. FE_TS gate: frontend tests pass
  9. CR gate: code review passed
  10. MD gate: app builds, tests pass
  11. MD_TS gate: mobile tests pass
  12. CR gate: code review passed
  13. BRU gate: business requirements met
  14. CRU gate: code requirements met
  15. MANUAL gate: manual acceptance passed
  16. VR gate: final verification passed

Rules:
  [F1] Flow MUST be followed in order — no skipping stages.
  [F2] Each implementation stage MUST be followed by its test suite.
  [F3] Each test suite MUST be followed by code review.
  [F4] Only changed files are tested in test suites.
  [F5] BRU requires human approval — AI MUST NOT auto-approve.
  [F6] CRU is automated — runs code quality and compliance checks.
  [F7] MANUAL requires user login with full permissions from environment.

State: +
